WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.880
A drop of pond water can look completely clear.

2
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:13.140
Put it under a microscope, and you may see tiny living things swimming and turning.

3
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.860
How can we know something is alive if it is too small to see?

4
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:20.943
Your eyes have a limit.

5
00:00:21.843 --> 00:00:26.543
Most people cannot see an object smaller than about one-tenth of a millimetre.

6
00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:30.623
A micrometre is one thousandth of a millimetre.

7
00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:34.383
So the limit is about 100 micrometres.

8
00:00:35.663 --> 00:00:37.623
Most cells are smaller than that.

9
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:41.193
A microscope is a tool with lenses.

10
00:00:41.893 --> 00:00:44.293
It makes small things look larger.

11
00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:50.253
Magnification is how many times larger the image looks than the real thing.

12
00:00:51.153 --> 00:00:57.533
A school microscope has an eyepiece that magnifies ten times. Its objective lenses

13
00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:00.813
are often four, ten, and forty times.

14
00:01:01.753 --> 00:01:07.253
Multiply them. That gives forty, one hundred, or four hundred times in all.

15
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:14.037
A light microscope can show details down to about 0.2 micrometres.

16
00:01:14.777 --> 00:01:17.297
That is enough to see most whole cells.

17
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:21.297
Later, scientists built the electron microscope.

18
00:01:22.097 --> 00:01:24.957
It uses a beam of electrons, not light.

19
00:01:25.897 --> 00:01:29.717
It showed cell parts far too small for any light microscope.

20
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:35.530
A cell is the smallest unit that can carry out the processes of life.

21
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.430
The cell theory sums up what scientists have learned about cells.

22
00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.230
It has three parts.

23
00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:47.210
First, all living things are made of one or more cells.

24
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.450
Second, the cell is the basic unit of life.

25
00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.310
Third, all cells come from cells that already exist.

26
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.980
In science, a theory is a well-tested explanation backed by a great deal of

27
00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.920
evidence. It is not a guess.

28
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.500
The cell theory grew as better microscopes gave new evidence.

29
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.180
So how do we know something is alive when it is too small to see?

30
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.620
A microscope makes it look large enough to see.

31
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.400
It shows that each one is made of one or more cells.
